From 3ff0865346ef57390a415429e4599da229749e33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 01:30:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] services: optional legacy Bluetooth input mode

Hades runs BlueZ with its secure input defaults: only bonded devices may
send input (genuine PS3 controllers paired with a USB cable are handled by
BlueZ as cable-paired devices) and re-pairing an already paired device must
be confirmed. LibreELEC instead accepted input from devices that never
bonded and re-paired silently, which lets anyone nearby inject key presses.

Add a "Legacy input devices (less secure)" switch that restores the
LibreELEC behaviour for devices that cannot bond, such as PS3 controller
clones. It is stored as BLUEZ_LEGACY_INPUT in the bluez service file, from
which Hades generates the BlueZ configuration.
